From: Codex-Android-DevOPS
 <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:16:32 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): let a reverse list with a known exact size shrink past
 the compose offset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

calculateAndUpdateContentSize grows a shrinking content size back to
composeOffset + viewport whenever the Compose offset lies past the new
maximum. On a reverse list that state means the native fling has run past
the oldest item into the 3000dp placeholder; growing it back keeps the
placeholder frame for the whole gesture. Device probe on botiverse/mobile
alpha 10020010 (raft.15): contentH held at 7058 for 40 frames of one fling
while rowsInView fell 14 -> 0 and the uncovered viewport grew to 933 px,
shrinking to 3749 only at scroll end.

When the exact size is known, a reverse list now shrinks; the re-anchor
(immediate for a shrink since #209) clamps the native offset to the real
end. Normal lists and an open estimate keep the existing behaviour.

Fork-Patch: compose-reverse-lazy-shrink-past-compose-offset
Origin: botiverse/mobile task #37 (fast-fling blank rows in thread)
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: Codex-Android-DevOPS (林舟) <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
index 456b79eaec5464fc77f601072ea860ef16a1ca84..ffdd1411768bb99420c162b3a2dd6f94cdf38ea8 100644
--- a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
+++ b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
@@ -127,6 +127,20 @@ internal object ReverseScrollOffsetMapping {
         )
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Whether a shrinking content size must instead grow to keep the current Compose offset
+     * inside the range (the default for every list).
+     *
+     * Not for a reverse list whose exact content size is known: there the Compose offset only
+     * lies past the new maximum because the native fling ran on into the placeholder content
+     * (`DEFAULT_CONTENT_SIZE`) beyond the oldest item. Keeping the placeholder frame lets the
+     * fling continue through a region with no rows for the whole gesture (botiverse/mobile
+     * task #37: contentH held at the placeholder for 40 frames while the viewport emptied);
+     * shrinking lets the re-anchor clamp the native offset to the real end instead.
+     */
+    fun keepContentSizeForComposeOffset(reverseLayout: Boolean, exactContentSizeKnown: Boolean): Boolean =
+        !(reverseLayout && exactContentSizeKnown)
+
     /**
      * Whether a non-forced re-anchor of a reverse list may be deferred to the end of the
      * active scroll stream instead of replaying every placed child per scroll event.
diff --git a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/scroller/ContentSizeExtensions.kt b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/scroller/ContentSizeExtensions.kt
index 85e911cec1c9452e0dd74b41290279fae3e95d8a..3805116d80cb688c3239766027d8bf19bac76cb5 100644
--- a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/scroller/ContentSizeExtensions.kt
+++ b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/scroller/ContentSizeExtensions.kt
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ import com.tencent.kuikly.compose.ui.unit.LayoutDirection
 import com.tencent.kuikly.compose.ui.util.fastSumBy
 import kotlinx.coroutines.delay
 import kotlinx.coroutines.launch
+import com.tencent.kuikly.compose.gestures.ReverseScrollOffsetMapping
 import kotlin.math.max
 import kotlin.math.roundToInt
 
@@ -97,7 +98,12 @@ internal fun ScrollableState.calculateAndUpdateContentSize(reanchorReverse: Bool
     // 如果contentSize变小了，需要确保composeOffset不会超出边界
     if (newContentSize < oldContentSize) {
         val newMaxScrollOffset = maxOf(0, newContentSize - kuiklyInfo.viewportSize)
-        if (kuiklyInfo.composeOffset > newMaxScrollOffset) {
+        if (kuiklyInfo.composeOffset > newMaxScrollOffset &&
+            ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.keepContentSizeForComposeOffset(
+                reverseLayout = kuiklyInfo.reverseLayout,
+                exactContentSizeKnown = kuiklyInfo.realContentSize != null,
+            )
+        ) {
             // 如果composeOffset超出新的边界，增加contentSize来保持composeOffset不变
             val requiredContentSize = kuiklyInfo.composeOffset.toInt() + kuiklyInfo.viewportSize
             kuiklyInfo.currentContentSize = maxOf(newContentSize, requiredContentSize)
diff --git a/compose/src/commonTest/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMappingTest.kt b/compose/src/commonTest/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMappingTest.kt
